{title: Lord, Whose Love Through Humble Service}
{key: C}
{time: 3/4}

{start_of_verse: 1}
Lord, whose [G]love through humble [Am]service bore the [F]weight of human [C]need
Who up[G]on the cross for[Am]saken, offered [F]mercy's perfect [C]deed
We, your [G]servants, bring the [Am]worship not of [Em]voice alone, but [F]heart
Conse[Am]crating to your [Dm]purpose every [F]gift that you im[C]part.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Still Your [G]children wander [Am]homeless; still the [F]hungry cry for [C]bread
Still the [G]captives long for [Am]freedom; still in [F]grief we mourn our [C]dead
As, O [G]Lord, your deep com[Am]passion, healed the [Em]sick and freed the [F]soul
Use the [Am]love Your Spirit [Dm]kindles, still to [F]save and make us [C]whole.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
As we [G]worship, grant us [Am]vision, till Your [F]love's revealing [C]light
In its [G]height and depth and [Am]greatness, dawns u[F]pon our quickened [C]sight
Making [G]known the needs and [Am]burdens Your com[Em]passion bids us [F]bear
Stirring [Am]us to tireless [Dm]striving, your a[F]bundant life to [C]share.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
Called by [G]worship to Your [Am]service, forth in [F]Your dear name we [C]go
To the [G]child, the youth, the [Am]aged, love in [F]living deeds to [C]show
Hope and [G]health, goodwill and [Am]comfort, counsel, [Em]aid, and peace we [F]give
That Your [Am]servants, Lord, in [Dm]freedom May Your [F]mercy know and [C]live.
{end_of_verse}
